   "source": [
    "String columns in real data are almost always messy — extra spaces, inconsistent casing, mixed formats."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "75d75e95",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Basic Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5bb6ca9f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasciencedojo/datasets/master/titanic.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(url)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "481e52aa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Create a messy example"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "09c63bda",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"city\"] = [\" Karachi\" , \"LAHORE\" , \"Islamabad\" , \"karachi\" , \"lahore\"]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c4f9b608",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Strip whitespace"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7e691447",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"city\"] = df[\"city\"].str.strip()\n",
    "# removes leading and trailing spaces\n",
    "df[\"city\"] = df[\"city\"].str.lstrip()     \n",
    "# leading only\n",
    "df[\"city\"] = df[\"city\"].str.rstrip()\n",
    "# trailing only"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "68f5e660",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Standardize case"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6f0485c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"city\"] = df[\"city\"].str.upper() # Upper Case\n",
    "df[\"city\"] = df[\"city\"].str.lower() # Lower Case\n",
    "df[\"city\"] = df[\"city\"].str.title() # Title case"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "66df7feb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "After cleaning: [\"Karachi\", \"Lahore\", \"Islamabad\", \"Karachi\", \"Lahore\"]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fa631c11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Replace specific values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d4278bad",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"city\"] = df[\"city\"].str.replace(\"Khi\" , \"Karachi\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eff40b46",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Check if contains a substring"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0b071a1a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[df[\"Name\"].str.contains(\"Mr\\.\", na=False)] # All Male Passengers"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "462917ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Extract parts of a string"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c4da45a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df[\"Title\"] = df[\"Name\"].str.extract(r\",\\s([A-Za-z]+)\\.\")\n",
    "# Extracts: Mr, Mrs, Miss, Dr, etc. from names like \"Braund, Mr. Owen\""
   ]
  },
